
class Solution {
    public int searchInsert(int[] nums, int target) {

        // left pointer starts at beginning of array
        int left = 0;

        // right pointer starts at last index of array
        int right = nums.length - 1;

        // Binary Search loop runs while left pointer is less than or equal to right
        while (left <= right) {

            // Find the middle index
            int mid = (left + right) / 2;

            // If target is found at mid, return its index
            if (nums[mid] == target) {
                return mid;
            }

            // If target is greater than middle element
            // move search to the right half
            else if (nums[mid] < target) {
                left = mid + 1;
            }

            // If target is smaller than middle element
            // move search to the left half
            else {
                right = mid - 1;
            }
        }

        // System.gc() forces garbage collection (not needed here)
        System.gc();

        // If target is not found, left will be the correct
        // position where the target should be inserted
        return left;
    }
}

When the loop ends:

left = correct insert position

because the search space collapses to where the target should be.

Example
nums = [1,3,5,6]
target = 2

Steps:

left	right	mid	nums[mid]	action
0	3	1	3	move left side → right=0
0	0	0	1	move right side → left=1

Loop ends → return left = 1.

Insert 2 at index 1.
